/target
# real secrets, referenced from config files as ${NAME}; see
# example_config/secrets.example.json. Nothing named secrets.json is committed,
# anywhere — the example_config one holds only the docker-compose password and is
# still ignored, because the rule is worth more than the one file it costs.
secrets.json
# what `just dev` passes as --data-dir: pipeline data written by file outputs.
# It is output, not a fixture, and a dev run can fill it without limit.
/dev_data
.playwright-mcp/
# the doc site's build output and dependencies. Everything *generated from the
# Rust source* under website/reference/generated is committed on purpose — it
# is what lets the site build without a toolchain, and a test compares it
# against the schemas.
/website/node_modules
/website/.vitepress/dist
/website/.vitepress/cache
